Introduction
************

This project was born out of a personal necessity: I needed to stop
bleeding money on home heating.

At first, I tried the standard route-using a smartphone app to schedule
the boiler.  But I quickly learned that savings were inversely
proportional to comfort.  My partner and I would celebrate a lower gas
bill while shivering in extra sweaters.

With a radiator system and a hybrid boiler, we ran the gamut of options:
hourly scheduling, integrated weather compensation curves, and
continuous low-power operation.  Nothing worked.  It was a binary choice
between comfort or savings; there was simply no middle ground.

* Menu:

* The Search for Intelligence::
* The Pivot: Programmable Intent::
* Giving Back to the Community::


File: starter-core.info,  Node: The Search for Intelligence,  Next: The Pivot: Programmable Intent,  Up: Introduction

The Search for Intelligence
===========================

I looked for off-the-shelf solutions to make the boiler "smarter," but I
hit a dead end.  While there were plugins available to _control_ the
hardware, the actual "intelligence" was missing.  I thought: _"We live
in the age of AI-why can't we apply that to home automation?"_

That’s when the project truly began.  My initial plan was to use a
"Lite" version of TensorFlow.  Since I'm not wealthy and couldn't afford
powerful servers, I invested my expertise instead of my cash.  I
envisioned a core that could toggle between "learning mode" and "active
mode."  It was an exciting prospect, but the AI path proved rocky.  It
required massive amounts of training data, and the results were
unpredictable.  I couldn't risk spending the rest of the winter in the
cold just for a neural network experiment.


File: starter-core.info,  Node: The Pivot: Programmable Intent,  Prev: The Search for Intelligence,  Up: Introduction

The Pivot: Programmable Intent
==============================

I decided to strip the problem down to its core objective: _Giving the
system clear instructions on how to behave based on the environment_.

To give instructions, you need to communicate.  To communicate, you need
a "channel" and a "protocol".  I realized the channel could be a simple
file, and the protocol a straightforward, human-readable language.  This
was the breakthrough that finally hit the target: _halving energy
consumption while actually increasing comfort_.

I achieved this through two fundamental logic rules:

_Efficiency Switching_
     Force the system to gas-only mode the moment environmental
     conditions make the heat pump inefficient.
_Dynamic Flow Control_
     Set the boiler's flow temperature based on:
        * A weighted average of the forecasted daily temperature swings.
        * A calculated offset based on a physical constant I discovered
          for my home: at 0^\circC outdoors, a 48^\circC flow
          temperature perfectly balances the house's heat loss.

Beyond Heating: The Monero Bonus
================================

Once the core was stable, more automations followed.  The most
satisfying one?  Managing my photovoltaic surplus.  When my solar panels
are overproducing and the grid voltage spikes near 250V, the system
automatically triggers my mining rigs to mine Monero.  It’s the ultimate
way to turn excess voltage into digital value.


File: starter-core.info,  Node: Giving Back to the Community,  Up: Introduction

Giving Back to the Community
============================

I believe this system has applications far beyond my own living room.
I’m sharing it so others can benefit from these optimizations just as I
have.

I am a firm believer in "Free Software" (in the true Stallman sense),
and this is my contribution to the community.  To ensure it remains free
and open for everyone to improve, I am distributing the Core under the
GPL license and the Library under the LGPL.


