B.7.2 STClient: Consuming a Service
-----------------------------------

The 'STClient' is the counterpart to the server.  It connects to a
remote 'STServer' and creates a local proxy of all its inputs, outputs,
and statistics.

 -- Function: STClient * st_client_new (void)
     Creates a new, uninitialized client object.

 -- Function: gboolean st_client_start (STClient *SELF, const gchar
          *ADDRESS, guint16 PORT, GError **ERROR)
     Connects the client to a remote service at the given ADDRESS and
     PORT.  Upon success, the client will automatically synchronize all
     remote I/O objects.

